# Chatwoot Core Guidelines

## Approach

- MVP focus: least code change, happy-path only
- No unnecessary defensive programming
- Ship the happy path first; add guards only when production proves they are needed
- Prefer minimal, readable code over abstractions
- Break complex tasks into small, testable units
- Iterate after confirmation
- Avoid writing specs unless explicitly asked
- Remove dead/unreachable/unused code
- Pick one approach — no duplicate versions of the same logic

## Commits

- Use Conventional Commits: `type(scope): subject`
- Example: `feat(auth): add user authentication`
- Do not reference Claude in commit messages

## Translations

- Only update `en.yml` (backend) and `en.json` (frontend)
- Other languages are handled by the community

## Frontend

- Use `components-next/` for message bubbles (the rest is being deprecated)

## Branding

- For user-facing strings containing "Chatwoot", use `replaceInstallationName` from `shared/composables/useBranding` instead of hardcoded brand copy
